🚀 Week 5 – Day 1 Java Packages: Built-in & User-defined ☕

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🧠 Introduction

Packages in Java are used to organize related classes and interfaces.

👉 Packages help in:

✔ Code organization
✔ Avoiding name conflicts
✔ Access control
✔ Reusability

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

📦 1. What is a Package?

A package is a collection of related classes, interfaces, and sub-packages.

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

📌 Syntax

```java id="p1"
package packageName;
```

---

📌 Example

```java id="p2"
package mypackage;

class Demo {
    void show() {
        System.out.println("Inside Package");
    }
}
```

---

🎯 Advantages of Packages

✔ Better code management
✔ Avoids class name conflicts
✔ Provides access protection
✔ Makes large projects manageable

---

🏗️ 2. Types of Packages

1️⃣ Built-in Packages
2️⃣ User-defined Packages

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🔹 3. Built-in Packages

Java provides many predefined packages.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

📊 Common Built-in Packages

| Package     | Purpose                       |
| ----------- | ----------------------------- |
| `java.lang` | Core language classes         |
| `java.util` | Utility classes & collections |
| `java.io`   | Input/output operations       |
| `java.sql`  | Database connectivity         |
| `java.net`  | Networking                    |

---

📌 Example

```java id="b1"
import java.util.Scanner;

class Test {
    public static void main(String[] args) {

        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);

        int num = sc.nextInt();

        System.out.println(num);
    }
}
```

---

🔍 import Statement

Used to access classes from packages.

```java id="b2"
import java.util.Scanner;
```

OR

```java id="b3"
import java.util.*;
```

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🔹 4. User-defined Packages

Packages created by programmers.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

📌 Creating User-defined Package

```java id="u1"
package mypackage;

public class Message {

    public void show() {
        System.out.println("Hello from package");
    }
}
```

---

📌 Save File Structure

```text id="u2"
mypackage/
    Message.java
```

---

▶️ Compile Package

```bash id="u3"
javac -d . Message.java
```

---

▶️ Using Package Class

```java id="u4"
import mypackage.Message;

class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {

        Message obj = new Message();

        obj.show();
    }
}
```

---

▶️ Run Program

```bash id="u5"
java Main
```

---

🧩 Sub-Packages

Packages can contain sub-packages.

```java id="u6"
package com.company.project;
```

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

⚠️ Common Mistakes

❌ Wrong folder structure
❌ Missing package statement
❌ Incorrect import statement
❌ Forgetting `public` keyword

